WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.150
Fashion is one of

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.180
the fastest growing
industries on the planet.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:10.410
Around the world, 80 billion
new pieces of clothing

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.300
are sold every year,

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.203
400% more than just 40 years ago.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.320
Americans alone are buying
five times more garments

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.240
than in 1980.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.910
Now, a $1.3 trillion mega industry,

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:28.553
fashion employs more than
300 million people worldwide.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:32.580
Where other industries have
come apart at the seams,

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.550
clothing production has
doubled in the last 15 years.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.800
But it's a fashion statement

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.720
with a steep environmental price tag.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.870
Making one kilogram of
fabric produces 23 kilograms

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.830
of greenhouse gasses.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.900
Textile production generates
more carbon dioxide

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.740
than all international flights

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:54.550
and maritime shipping combined.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:58.480
Yet half of all clothes are
thrown away within one year,

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.110
many having never been worn.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:04.570
Fashion is now considered the
second most polluting industry

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:07.170
in the world after oil.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:10.040
And with increasing middle
classes in the developing world

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.700
keen to make their own fashion statement,

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.223
this will get worse.

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:18.450
If 80% of emerging markets
reach western levels

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.310
of clothes shopping,
carbon dioxide emissions

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:25.250
could increase by nearly 80% per person.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:30.250
By 2050 total clothing sales
could reach 175 million tons

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.350
turning the planet into
the biggest fashion victim

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:36.293
of them all.

